-- title:
--   Drinfeld upper half plane is exhausted by the standard affinoids
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K$, let $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$, and let $C$ be a field equipped with a valuation $v$ taking values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, together with a $K$-algebra structure; let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and over which $C$ is an algebra, with the scalar towers $\mathcal{O} \to R \to C$ and $\mathcal{O} \to K \to C$ compatible. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformizer, that is, an element $\varpi \in K$ with $0 < v(\varpi) < 1$ in $C$ such that for every nonzero $a \in K$ there is $N$ with $v(\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi)^{-N}$ (valuations of images in $C$ throughout). Assume `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`, i.e. $\pi$ is irreducible in $\mathcal{O}$; $R \to C$ is injective; its image is exactly $\{c \in C : v(c) \le 1\}$; $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; an element $a \in K$ satisfies $v(a) \le 1$ precisely when it comes from $\mathcal{O}$; the image of $K$ is closed in $C$; and $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. The conclusion is `IsExhausted ϖ`: every $z$ in the complement of the image of $K$ in $C$ lies in some standard affinoid, i.e. for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$ one has $v(z) \le v(\varpi)^{-n}$ and $v(\varpi)^n \le v(z - a)$ for every $a \in K$ with $v(a) \le v(\varpi)^{-n}$.
--
--   This is the statement that Drinfeld's $p$-adic upper half plane $\Omega = C \setminus K$ is the increasing union of the standard affinoids $\Omega_n$, in the axiomatic setting of an adic frame $(\pi, \varpi, R)$ for $C$. It is used in the analysis of points of the formal moduli functor, namely by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.AdicPoint.toOmega_surjOn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.AdicPoint.toOmega_surjOn).
